  "full_response": "No, vaccines do not cause autism. This claim has been thoroughly investigated and debunk by numerous scientific studies spanning multiple years and published in reputable journals. Originally, this association originated from a discredited study published by Andrew Wakefield in 1998. Subsequent large-scale studies, including those conducted by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) and the Institute of Medicine (now the National Academy of Medicine), have consistently found no link between vaccination and autism. Vaccines are safe and essential for protecting individuals and communities against various infectious diseases.",
